## Notes on two ACs called out by the calling command

- **AC-3** is written as a leak test, not an absence test: `test/export.test.ts`
  seeds `google_connections.refresh_token` and `push_subscriptions.p256dh`/`auth`
  with sentinel strings, fetches the export, and asserts the RAW response TEXT
  contains none of the three sentinel strings, in addition to asserting the
  three excluded table names carry no key in the parsed body.
- **AC-4** is written with the exclusion half as the point: alongside the
  real-schema enumeration assertion (`drizzle-orm`'s `is()`/`SQLiteTable`/
  `getTableConfig` over every exported value of `src/worker/db/schema.ts`),
  `test/export-completeness.test.ts` also proves the checking logic itself
  (`findUnaccountedTables` / `findUnreasonedExclusions`, written in the test
  file, not in production code) against small FIXTURE lists — one fixture with
  an unclassified table name, one fixture with a whitespace-only exclusion
  reason — so the guard's discriminative power is proven independently of
  whether today's real schema happens to already be complete.

